1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:04,647
After the flood, Noah's grandchildren
began to fall sick and die.

2
00:00:05,097 --> 00:00:08,690
Their fathers came to Noah.
Something, they said, is leading

3
00:00:08,690 --> 00:00:11,625
our children astray,
blinding them, killing them.

4
00:00:12,075 --> 00:00:14,498
The Book of Jubilees says angels gave Noah

5
00:00:14,498 --> 00:00:16,576
the cure, and he wrote it in a book.

6
00:00:17,026 --> 00:00:19,373
That book is lost. So what was in it?

7
00:00:21,323 --> 00:00:26,485
Jubilees retells Genesis as an angel's
words to Moses on Mount Sinai.

8
00:00:26,935 --> 00:00:31,053
The angel speaks as we. So in this
chapter, the narrator was there.

9
00:00:31,503 --> 00:00:35,535
Ethiopian Bibles call it Mets'hafe
Kufale, the Book of Division.

10
00:00:35,985 --> 00:00:38,481
And the whole book survives in only one

11
00:00:38,481 --> 00:00:41,041
language: Ge'ez. What did Noah do first?

12
00:00:42,991 --> 00:00:45,999
He prayed. God of the
spirits of all flesh, let

13
00:00:45,999 --> 00:00:48,175
not wicked spirits rule over them.

14
00:00:48,625 --> 00:00:51,722
He reminds God who fathered
these spirits: the

15
00:00:51,722 --> 00:00:54,214
Watchers, the fallen angels of Enoch.

16
00:00:54,664 --> 00:00:57,843
God answers. The angels
are told to bind them all.

17
00:00:58,293 --> 00:01:00,831
Then someone steps forward
to argue with God.

18
00:01:02,781 --> 00:01:05,192
It is the chief of the spirits, Mastema.

19
00:01:05,642 --> 00:01:08,467
Lord, Creator, he says, leave some of them

20
00:01:08,467 --> 00:01:10,485
to me, or I cannot do my work.

21
00:01:10,935 --> 00:01:14,519
His reason: great is the
wickedness of the sons of men.

22
00:01:14,969 --> 00:01:17,854
God allows one part in ten. Nine parts go

23
00:01:17,854 --> 00:01:20,387
down into the place of condemnation.

24
00:01:20,837 --> 00:01:25,189
So one spirit in ten is still loose.
What protects Noah's family now?

25
00:01:27,139 --> 00:01:30,446
One angel is sent to teach
Noah all their medicines.

26
00:01:30,896 --> 00:01:33,001
In the words of Jubilees: how he might

27
00:01:33,001 --> 00:01:34,885
heal them with herbs of the earth.

28
00:01:35,335 --> 00:01:39,175
Noah writes everything down, every
kind of medicine, in a book.

29
00:01:39,625 --> 00:01:42,932
He gives it to Shem, the son
he loved above all the others.

30
00:01:43,382 --> 00:01:46,536
Then Noah dies, at nine
hundred and fifty. And the

31
00:01:46,536 --> 00:01:49,249
book disappears from
the story. Or does it?

32
00:01:51,199 --> 00:01:54,800
Did you know? A medieval Hebrew
medical book, the Book of

33
00:01:54,800 --> 00:01:57,769
Asaph the Physician, opens
with the same story.

34
00:01:58,219 --> 00:02:00,715
There the angel has a name: Raphael.

35
00:02:01,165 --> 00:02:04,193
The cures come from trees,
plants and roots, and

36
00:02:04,193 --> 00:02:07,032
Noah's book passes to
the ancient physicians.

37
00:02:07,482 --> 00:02:11,279
Same flood, same Noah, same book.
So which telling came first?

38
00:02:13,229 --> 00:02:15,910
Scholars still argue. One thinks Jubilees

39
00:02:15,910 --> 00:02:18,264
knew of Noah's book only by hearsay.

40
00:02:18,714 --> 00:02:21,290
Another thinks Jubilees
played down the cures,

41
00:02:21,290 --> 00:02:23,194
so they would not look like magic.

42
00:02:23,644 --> 00:02:27,495
Hebrew pieces of about fifteen
Jubilees scrolls turned up at

43
00:02:27,495 --> 00:02:30,897
Qumran. The oldest are around
two thousand years old.

44
00:02:31,347 --> 00:02:34,001
A Latin copy in Milan
keeps about a third of

45
00:02:34,001 --> 00:02:35,870
the book, but not this chapter.

46
00:02:36,320 --> 00:02:39,235
Only the Ge'ez Bible keeps all of it, word

47
00:02:39,235 --> 00:02:41,525
for word, in Ethiopia's churches.

48
00:02:43,475 --> 00:02:46,362
Notice what Jubilees does not give us. No

49
00:02:46,362 --> 00:02:49,107
recipe, no spell, not one herb by name.

50
00:02:49,557 --> 00:02:52,480
It gives a prayer first, and
then healing from the earth.

51
00:02:52,930 --> 00:02:55,068
Sirach says it plainly: the Lord hath

52
00:02:55,068 --> 00:02:57,090
created medicines out of the earth.

53
00:02:57,540 --> 00:02:59,995
So when a post promises a secret ancient

54
00:02:59,995 --> 00:03:02,020
cure, ask who wrote it, and when.

55
00:03:03,970 --> 00:03:08,045
Noah did two things. He prayed, and
he wrote down what he was taught.

56
00:03:08,495 --> 00:03:11,708
We swing between fear that
sees a spirit behind every

57
00:03:11,708 --> 00:03:14,617
fever, and pride that
thinks it needs no prayer.

58
00:03:15,067 --> 00:03:18,279
The quiet path is older:
pray, take the medicine, sit

59
00:03:18,279 --> 00:03:20,763
with the sick, and leave the rest to God.

60
00:03:21,213 --> 00:03:24,477
Maybe tonight we pray for
one sick person, by name.

61
00:03:26,427 --> 00:03:28,518
Thank you for sitting with us over coffee.

62
00:03:28,968 --> 00:03:30,440
This is Ethiopics.
